Package: multiomeFate
Title: Clonal Fate Estimation by Exponential Regression ('CYFER')
Version: 1.0.3.000
Authors@R: c(person("Kevin", "Lin",  role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "kzlin@uw.edu"),
    person("Xinyi", "Chen", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates a per-cell fate potential, the expected number of
    progeny a cell contributes to a designated future population, from
    lineage-barcoded single-cell data. A Poisson generalized linear model with a
    log-linear mean is fit to per-clone counts at the later time point using
    features measured only at the earlier time point, so that clonal expansion
    and intra-clonal heterogeneity are modelled explicitly and the estimate
    survives a selection bottleneck. Also provides the lineage-barcode assignment
    pipeline, simulation generators, and plotting helpers used in Chen, Lin,
    Schaff et al., "Resolution of Selection Versus Adaptation in Cellular
    Evolution".
Depends:
    R (>= 3.5.0)
